$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure II ( for cat.2, cat4, cat.7-9) N-Cbz-amino acid (10
mmol) was dissolved in THF (25 mL) and cooled in an ice bath. NMM (10
mmol) and ethyl chloroformate ( 10 mmol) were added to the aboved cooled
solution and stirred for 30min. The resulting mixture was treated with
sulfonyl hydrazide (1.2 eq, 12mmol) or hydroxylamine derivatives at 0 °C.
After 2h the solvent THF was evaporated and the residue was dissolved in
DCM (200 mL). Then the DCM layer was washed with hydrogen chloride
solution (2M, 60×3 mL) and brine subsequently. The solvent was dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4 and evaporated in vacuum. The crude product which could
be used in next step directly. The deprotection of the above crude
product was performed in the presence of Pd/C (1mmol, 10 mol%) in
methanol (50 mmol) under the atmosphere of hydrogen. The resulting
mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. When the reaction
completed, the reaction mixture was filtered and the solvent was removed
in vacuum. The obtained mixture was further purified by flash
chromatography ( DCM/Methanol = 20/1 ).
(S)-N'-(2-amino-3-phenylpropanoyl)-4-methylbenzenesulfonohydrazide
(cat.2): white solid in 93 % yield. M.p. 112-115 °C. [α]D 20 -61.5 (c =
1.1, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.78-7.76 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H),
7.29-7.23 (m, 5H), 7.13-7.11 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 3.60-3.59 (m, 1H)
2.97-2.93 (dd, J = 4.0 Hz, J = 14.0 Hz, 1H), 2.51-2.44 (dd, J = 10 Hz, J
= 19.2 Hz, 1H), 2.40 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 172.51,144.85,
136.77, 133.36, 129. 53, 129.16, 128.81, 128.62, 127.07, 55.47, 40.45,
21.68; IR (film, ν/cm-1 ): 3217, 3030, 2924, 2845, 1679, 1597, 1495,
1341, 1163, 1089, 814, 700; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C16H19N3O3S [M+H]+
334.1225, found 334.1225.
